  "problem": "A numerical method is used to approximate a solution to an initial value problem, resulting in the table below. If the exact solution is $y(x)=\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}},$ find, rounded to three decimal places, the global truncation error at each step.\n\n| $n$ | ${x}_{n}$ | ${y}_{n}$ | ${e}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.25$ | $1.030$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $2$ | $0.5$ | $1.100$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $3$ | $0.75$ | $1.230$ | {{field-3}} |",
